  Sum of last digit of two given numbers


import java.util.Scanner;

public class SumOfLastDigits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter first number: ");
        int num1 = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.print("Enter second number: ");
        int num2 = sc.nextInt();

        int lastDigit1 = num1 % 10;
        int lastDigit2 = num2 % 10;

        int sum = lastDigit1 + lastDigit2;

        System.out.println("Sum of last digits = " + sum);

        sc.close();
    }
}


Sample Output
Enter first number: 123
Enter second number: 456
Sum of last digits = 9
Result

The program was executed successfully and the sum of the last digits of the two given numbers was found.
